+      "body": "I was nineteen when our Higgins boat dropped its ramp on Omaha Beach. Forty-four years later I can still hear the engines and feel the cold Channel water. Half the boys from my squad never made it past the shingle. I go back every few years to Normandy to stand at the cemetery at Colleville and read the names. To the young folks here: freedom was bought at a price, and I have spent my life trying to be worthy of the men who paid it. God rest them all.",
