+      "subject": "RE: Revolutionary War pension files -- what is actually in them?",
+      "body": "RevWarRick, order it -- pension files are genealogy gold. A Revolutionary War pension file (the M804 microfilm series) can run 20 to 60 pages: the veteran's own narrative of his service, affidavits from comrades, marriage records, children's birth dates, and sometimes letters in the widow's hand. The NATF Form 80 costs $10 and you mail it to Washington. Be patient -- turnaround is several weeks. One file broke a ten-year brick wall for me with a single deposition naming four siblings.",
