+      "subject": "Layering DX7 and D-50 -- MIDI channel setup",
+      "body": "Finally have both a Yamaha DX7 and a Roland D-50 in the home studio and I want to layer them from one keyboard. The plan: DX7 as master on channel 1, D-50 receiving on channel 1 with local off, then split the D-50's upper/lower across two channels for sequencer overdubs. For those running a two-keyboard MIDI rig: any gotchas with the D-50's patch changes eating the DX7's program changes? And is anyone using a dedicated MIDI patchbay, or just daisy-chaining thru ports?",
